MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Breaks the SDL/0050 quiescence-gate × DOS cooperative-scheduler
deadlock on Quit-to-DOS without sacrificing the +7 fps gain.

The bug (iter L L1 / iter M M1 2026-05-08, both freeze): SDL/0050's
GetDeviceBuf quiescence-walk path calls SDL_Delay(10) under the
audio thread's hold of device->lock (lock taken at SDL_audio.c:1179,
not released until 1289). When the engine calls MIX_DestroyMixer,
main blocks at SDL_LockMutex(device->lock) in DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice
at line 586 BEFORE reaching the atomic shutdown=1 set at line 1668.
Under DOS cooperative scheduling, audio's end-of-Iterate unlock →
next-Iterate re-lock cycle re-acquires the lock before main wins the
spin-loop race. Main starves indefinitely. SDL/0051's atomic-bypass
at top of GetDeviceBuf is dead code because the atomic is INSIDE the
lock main can't acquire.

The fix: engine flips the SDL/0050 killswitch state from
SoundManager::shutdown() immediately before MIX_DestroyMixer via a
new workspace-local export, SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(). After the
flip, the next GetDeviceBuf takes the default-path return (staging
buffer unchanged, no SDL_Delay). Audio thread cycles fast; lock is
held only for the µs-class mix work; main wins lock contention in
≤10 ms; sets shutdown=1; SDL_WaitThread joins cleanly.

Reuses the existing g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled flag rather
than introducing a parallel g_dos_audio_shutting_down state — avoids
the gate-fragmentation footgun documented in the SDL/0048 follow-up
work (memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md). One flag,
one semantic ("gate is off"), set by either OpenDevice-time hint
resolution or this engine-signaled mid-run flip.

Zero risk to the +7 fps gain. The flag is only flipped during the
engine's shutdown call. Gameplay-time path (gate engaged, fires
SDL_Delay when quiescent) is byte-identical to current. Flag-check
cost is one static-bool read; already in the current path.

Engine-side companion: nxengine-evo adds a 5-LOC call to
SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown() between the existing
snd-shutdown[3/6]/[4/6] markers in SoundManager::shutdown(). Header
declares the symbol via include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h
(workspace-local; mirrors SDL/0034's SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h
pattern).

DOSBox-X smoke can validate structurally (new path executes; log
markers emit; game still hits title) but cannot reliably reproduce
the cooperative-scheduler-vs-mutex contention timing per
dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md. The wave-33 quit-cycle PLAY
cell is the behavioral gate.

Per sdl_ai_policy.md the patch stays workspace-local; not for
upstream.

Files touched:
  vendor/SDL/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h     (new)
  vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c          (include +
                                                       ~10 LOC function +
                                                       inline reasoning)

Companion patches:
  SDL/0050 — DOS GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate (this patch unblocks
             its shutdown-path interaction)
  SDL/0051 — atomic-bypass-at-top (dead code; left in tree for
             documentation of the wrong-hypothesis attempt)
  SDL/0046 — WaitDevice shutdown bail (sibling deadlock fix, still
             needed for the non-quiescence WaitDevice path)
  nxengine-evo/0129 — companion call site
