    idle-pause coordination state. The public-API state vars are defined
@@ -819,6 +820,80 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     return true;
 }
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0053): engine-signaled pre-shutdown gate
+   disable. Called from the engine's SoundManager::shutdown() immediately
+   before MIX_DestroyMixer to break the SDL/0050 quiescence-gate × DOS
+   cooperative-scheduler deadlock on Quit-to-DOS.
+
+   The deadlock geometry (iter L L1 / iter M M1 + docs/PHASE11-ITER-M-
+   FREEZE-DIAGNOSTIC.md § 18):
+     1. SDL3 main thread enters MIX_DestroyMixer → SDL_QuitSubSystem
+        (or SDL_DestroyAudioStream for simplified-bound streams) →
+        DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice (SDL_audio.c:579).
+     2. DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice acquires device->lock at line 586
+        BEFORE calling ClosePhysicalAudioDevice. Main blocks here.
+     3. Audio thread holds device->lock for the entire body of
+        PlaybackAudioThreadIterate (SDL_audio.c:1179 → 1289) — including
+        DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf, where SDL/0050's quiescence-walk
+        path calls SDL_Delay(10) under cooperative scheduler.
+     4. Audio's end-of-Iterate SDL_UnlockMutex → next-Iterate
+        SDL_LockMutex cycle re-acquires the lock before main's spin
+        loop wins under DOS cooperative scheduling. Main starves; the
+        atomic shutdown=1 set at SDL_audio.c:1668 is INSIDE the lock
+        main cannot reach. SDL/0051's atomic-check-at-top-of-GetDeviceBuf
+        is dead code for the same reason.
+
+   The fix is to flip the gate's killswitch state from the engine BEFORE
+   main thread enters MIX_DestroyMixer. We reuse the existing
+   g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled flag (set/reset normally at
+   OpenDevice time via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE) rather
+   than introducing a parallel g_dos_audio_shutting_down state — this
+   avoids the gate-fragmentation footgun documented in
+   memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md (the SDL/0048
+   ForcePause-vs-force_dsp_pause split that bit us in iter J).
+
+   After the flag flips true, the next DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf
+   iteration takes the default-path return (staging_buffer unchanged,
+   no SDL_Delay). Audio thread cycles fast through Iterate; lock is
+   held only for the µs-class mix work; main wins the lock contention
+   within ≤10 ms (one residual SDL_Delay if the flip races mid-delay);
+   main sets shutdown=1, releases lock, calls SDL_WaitThread. Audio
+   thread's WaitDevice (SDL/0046 shutdown bail) returns true; next
+   Iterate observes shutdown=1, returns false; thread exits cleanly.
+
+   Lifecycle / idempotence:
+     - One-shot per process lifetime, but safe to call twice (no-op
+       redundant set).
+     - Safe when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 already
+       killswitched the gate at OpenDevice (flag already true).
+     - Safe when audio was never initialized (writes a static; no SDL
+       state dependency).
+     - DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice re-resolves the hint on each open,
+       so a hypothetical re-open in the same process resets cleanly
+       (Cave Story never does this).
+
+   Threading: aligned bool writes are atomic on x86 (DJGPP target).
+   Audio-thread readers see either the old or new value; a racing
+   reader observing old enters at most one more SDL_Delay(10) before
+   re-reading. No barrier required.
+
+   Per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md the patch stays workspace-local; the
+   exported symbol is declared in include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h
+   alongside the SDL_DOSVesaDirect* pattern from SDL/0034. */
+void SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(void)
+{
+    if (!g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled) {
+        g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled = true;
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown — gate disabled "
+                         "for shutdown lock-handoff (engine pre-empted "
+                         "SDL/0050 GetDeviceBuf quiescence walk before "
+                         "MIX_DestroyMixer)");
+    } else {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown — gate already "
+                         "disabled (killswitch or repeat call); no-op");
+    }
+}
+
 // Return the staging buffer. The SDL audio pipeline writes the mixed audio
 // here; PlayDevice then copies it into the ring buffer.
 static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_size)
